title: "How often W3C drafts become Recommendations"
abstract: "Fewer than half of the web standards W3C started in 2000-2014 became Recommendations within ten years. W3C now publishes about half as many Recommendations a year as in 2015-2019, but our prediction that the 2020 Process slowed specs down failed. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
